I was interested in getting a PSP for that exact reason, too. However,
like you said, the CURRENT implementation of Nethack requires almost
the oldest possible firmware version on the PSP.


Furthermore, from what I have been able to uncover, you are almost
forcibly coerced by Sony to upgrade your firmware in order to run some
of the newer software, and you CAN'T ever roll back your firmware
version once you have upgraded it - meaning, even if you find an old
one in a pawn shop, you may still be screwed trying to find one with
old firmware.


(I may be wrong - these things could have changed in the past few
months)


So, for now, unless someone has a new crack for the PSP, you can't run
Nethack unless you have an old, un-upgraded PSP, and the new PSP's all
have the most recent versions installed.


Hope this helps, and you haven't spent the money yet! And if I am
totally wrong, I would love to hear - I would buy a PSP, too, if I
could reliably get Nethack to run on it.



